  data: {
    LLM: "Memory is everything. Track which cards of matching ranks have already been captured so you don't save a card for a match that is impossible.\n\nUnder Yoruba rules, avoid making 'obvious' sums. If you have a 10, don't leave a 7 and 3 on the table for your opponent; try to scoop them yourself first.\n\nEsun Management: Build protected piles that require a high card (like a 10) to scoop, ensuring you have that 10 in hand before you start the pile. If an opponent sees your pile building, they may try to 'break' it by scooping components before you finish.",
    Player: "Memory is everything. Track which cards of matching ranks have already been captured so you don't save a card for a match that is impossible.\n\nUnder Yoruba rules, avoid making 'obvious' sums. If you have a 10, don't leave a 7 and 3 on the table for your opponent; try to scoop them yourself first.\n\nEsun Management: Build protected piles that require a high card (like a 10) to scoop, ensuring you have that 10 in hand before you start the pile. If an opponent sees your pile building, they may try to 'break' it by scooping components before you finish.",
