    basic: "Memory is everything. Track which cards of matching ranks have already been captured so you don't save a card for a match that is impossible.",
    intermediate: "Under Yoruba rules, avoid making 'obvious' sums. If you have a 10, don't leave a 7 and 3 on the table for your opponent; try to scoop them yourself first.",
    advanced: "Esun Management: Build protected piles that require a high card (like a 10) to scoop, ensuring you have that 10 in hand before you start the pile. If an opponent sees your pile building, they may try to 'break' it by scooping components before you finish.",
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "Face cards (K, Q, J) are 'dead weight' if their matches are gone. Dump them early if the table is clear of their rank.",
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'If playing with Isiwo, use it! Checking your pile helps you count the remaining ranks in the deck.',
